  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_006_TerminalWrongWifi
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-006
  title: Register sits there and won't ring anything up
  category: 0
  content: "A terminal can have perfectly good internet and still be unable to reach
    POS \u2014 if it joined the wrong Wi-Fi. Every nearby network hands out its own
    IP range, so joining the guest network (or the shop next door, or someone's hotspot)
    puts the terminal on a subnet POS cannot see.\nRead the store's real SSID in
    Network Settings, compare it with POS Terminal \u25B8 Status, and re-join the
    correct network. IP and gateway follow automatically \u2014 you never type those
    in. 'Not connecting' does not have to mean the network is down."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P6
